00:50:17.430 --> 00:50:24.450
I wrote in my MySpace blog about this moment, and I wrote that it was one of the hardest
我在我的MySpace博客里写过这一刻，我写道这是我们作为演员最难熬的时刻之一，

1252
00:50:24.450 --> 00:50:31.790
things for us to get through as a cast, that the first time Mindy unrolls the poster and
因为当敏迪第一次展开那张海报，

1253
00:50:31.790 --> 00:50:33.870
looks at it, and we all see it.
看着它，我们所有人都看到了。

1254
00:50:34.070 --> 00:50:37.130
We all, every person lost it.
我们所有人，每个人都笑场了。

1255
00:50:37.130 --> 00:50:38.750
Because it's so ridiculous.
因为它太荒谬了。

1256
00:50:38.750 --> 00:50:39.630
It's so ridiculous.
太荒谬了。

1257
00:50:39.630 --> 00:50:41.050
We had not seen it.
我们之前没见过它。

1258
00:50:41.330 --> 00:50:47.350
It was an actual surprise to us while we were filming, and we all lost it.
拍摄时这对我们来说是个真正的惊喜，我们全都笑喷了。

1259
00:50:47.890 --> 00:50:54.210
I had that, in fact, it was particularly hard on Rain for some reason, and that in one take,
我记得，事实上，不知为何这对雷恩来说特别难，在其中一条拍摄中，

1260
00:50:54.210 --> 00:50:57.610
he broke three times because he could not get through it.
他笑场了三次，因为他实在演不下去。

1261
00:50:57.610 --> 00:51:03.490
I can't believe that Mindy was tasked with having to unroll that poster.
我真不敢相信敏迪竟然被指派去展开那张海报。

1262
00:51:03.890 --> 00:51:06.530
How did we ever get a shot of her not laughing?
我们到底是怎么拍到她没笑的镜头的？

1263
00:51:06.790 --> 00:51:09.370
I don't know, but we were cracking up.
我不知道，但我们当时都快笑死了。

1264
00:51:09.550 --> 00:51:13.530
There's a little detail in that scene that made me laugh when I rewatched it, which is how you
那场戏里有个小细节让我重看时又笑了，就是你

1265
00:51:13.530 --> 00:51:18.410
just very subtly swat the oven mitt away on your way to getting the poster.
在去拿海报的路上，非常微妙地把隔热手套拍开。

1266
00:51:18.650 --> 00:51:19.430
That was all me.
那是我自己加的。

1267
00:51:19.610 --> 00:51:20.510
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

1268
00:51:20.550 --> 00:51:22.110
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

1269
00:51:22.110 --> 00:51:23.750
It was such a good detail.
那真是个很棒的细节。

1270
00:51:24.010 --> 00:51:24.750
I loved it.
我很喜欢。

1271
00:51:27.250 --> 00:51:32.430
Well, in tracking the oven mitt, Meredith eventually takes the oven mitt.
嗯，说到那个隔热手套，梅雷迪斯最后拿走了它。

1272
00:51:33.450 --> 00:51:39.370
But, you know, Michael has to then call her a sucker and say that he wanted her to take it,
但是，你知道，迈克尔随后得叫她傻瓜，说他本来就想让她拿走，

1273
00:51:39.410 --> 00:51:42.310
and it was reverse psychology when he said he wanted to keep it.
还说他之前说想留着它其实是反向心理。

1274
00:51:42.470 --> 00:51:46.770
I love that he decided that he needed to break down reverse psychology to all of us,
我喜欢他决定要向我们所有人解释什么是反向心理，

1275
00:51:46.790 --> 00:51:47.970
because I don't know if you've heard of it.
因为我不知道你们有没有听说过这个词。

1276
00:51:48.110 --> 00:51:49.410
This is a pretty cool thing.
这可是个很酷的东西。

1277
00:51:49.790 --> 00:51:51.670
I'm like, Michael, you're such an idiot.
我当时心想，迈克尔，你真是个白痴。

1278
00:51:51.670 --> 00:51:56.750
Do you remember how Phyllis cried during that scene?
你还记得菲利斯在那场戏里是怎么哭的吗？

1279
00:51:57.030 --> 00:52:00.010
Yeah, she stayed in, like, sort of that sad place.
记得，她一直沉浸在那种悲伤的情绪里。

1280
00:52:00.250 --> 00:52:05.530
She cried for, like, a half hour, and in between takes of that, where she had to be crying,
她哭了大概半小时，在需要哭戏的拍摄间隙，

1281
00:52:05.690 --> 00:52:07.050
she didn't want any of us to talk to her.
她不想让我们任何人跟她说话。

1282
00:52:07.110 --> 00:52:09.010
And Kate and I tried to go up and give her a hug.
凯特和我试着走过去想给她一个拥抱。

1283
00:52:09.270 --> 00:52:10.410
She didn't want it.
她拒绝了。

1284
00:52:10.490 --> 00:52:12.350
Like, she was in this, like, actor zone.
她当时完全进入了那种演员的专注状态。

1285
00:52:12.510 --> 00:52:14.270
It's so hard to do.
这真的很难做到。

1286
00:52:14.690 --> 00:52:15.910
It's so hard to do.
这真的很难做到。

1287
00:52:16.030 --> 00:52:19.390
I know exactly where she was, but I just remember being really worried for her,
我完全理解她的状态，但我只记得当时真的很为她担心，

1288
00:52:19.390 --> 00:52:24.310
because when you see Phyllis cry, it is, ugh.
因为当你看到菲利斯哭的时候，哎呀。

1289
00:52:24.710 --> 00:52:26.030
You don't want to see Phyllis cry.
你根本不想看到菲利斯哭。

1290
00:52:26.030 --> 00:52:27.170
You don't want to see her cry.
你不想看到她哭。

1291
00:52:27.170 --> 00:52:28.730
Because it breaks every part of you open.
因为那会让你心碎不已。

1292
00:52:28.730 --> 00:52:30.390
I mean, she did.
我是说，她确实做到了。

1293
00:52:30.530 --> 00:52:37.270
She had to stay sad, and it is really hard, especially sitting in this circle with people
她必须保持悲伤，这真的很难，尤其是在这个圈子里，大家都在

1294
00:52:37.270 --> 00:52:39.310
cracking up about a baby poster.
因为一张婴儿海报而笑得前仰后合。

1295
00:52:39.450 --> 00:52:39.610
Yeah.
是啊。

1296
00:52:39.610 --> 00:52:41.890
But you've got to stay sad.
但你必须保持悲伤。

1297
00:52:42.190 --> 00:52:42.510
Yes.
没错。

1298
00:52:42.750 --> 00:52:43.410
It's hard.
这很难。

1299
00:52:43.650 --> 00:52:44.250
It's really hard.
真的很难。

1300
00:52:44.390 --> 00:52:44.890
That is very difficult.
那非常困难。

1301
00:52:45.410 --> 00:52:46.570
Well, here's the thing.
是这样的。

1302
00:52:46.830 --> 00:52:48.690
Michael just gets progressively meaner.
迈克尔变得越来越刻薄了。

1303
00:52:48.870 --> 00:52:54.090
You know, he calls Meredith a sucker, and then Dwight, you know, he opens the paintball,
你知道，他叫梅雷迪思“笨蛋”，然后德怀特，你知道，他打开了彩弹枪，

1304
00:52:54.270 --> 00:52:57.630
and he's like, ugh, you know, how is this better than an iPod?
他说，呃，你知道，这怎么能比得上iPod呢？

1305
00:52:57.630 --> 00:53:02.390
And this moment kind of broke my heart, too, when Dwight goes, I never said it was better.
这一刻也让我有点心碎，当德怀特说，我从没说过它更好。

1306
00:53:02.610 --> 00:53:03.170
You know?
你懂吗？

1307
00:53:03.850 --> 00:53:06.570
Wait, I have an Angela pissed off in this moment.
等等，我这儿有一段安吉拉生气的画面。

1308
00:53:06.690 --> 00:53:07.370
Oh, okay, go.
哦，好的，开始吧。

1309
00:53:07.370 --> 00:53:11.790
At 13 minutes, 58 seconds, look at my face.
在13分58秒的时候，看我的表情。

1310
00:53:11.970 --> 00:53:13.310
I wrote it in all caps.
我用全大写字母写下来了。

1311
00:53:13.670 --> 00:53:19.710
So Michael has just called Meredith a sucker because she got the lame, you know, oven mitt,
迈克尔刚叫梅雷迪思“笨蛋”，因为她拿到了那个烂烤箱手套，

1312
00:53:19.890 --> 00:53:22.010
and Phyllis storms out, okay?
然后菲利斯冲了出去，好吗？

1313
00:53:22.270 --> 00:53:27.690
She is completely heartbroken now, and the party is falling apart, and the look on my face
她现在彻底心碎了，派对也乱成了一团，而我脸上的表情

1314
00:53:27.690 --> 00:53:31.250
is just sheer in, like, rage.
简直就是纯粹的，那种，愤怒。

1315
00:53:31.630 --> 00:53:33.670
Now, are we at the top of your rage now?
现在，你的愤怒达到顶峰了吗？

1316
00:53:33.830 --> 00:53:34.330
No.
没有。

1317
00:53:34.550 --> 00:53:35.010
Oh, no.
哦，没有。

1318
00:53:35.150 --> 00:53:37.190
Well, I mean, I know we've still got the parking lot.
我是说，我知道我们还有停车场那场戏。

1319
00:53:37.370 --> 00:53:38.530
But no, oh, no.
但不是现在，哦，不是。

1320
00:53:38.730 --> 00:53:40.670
There's a moment coming, and you'll know it.
有一个时刻即将到来，你会知道的。

1321
00:53:40.910 --> 00:53:45.850
It's the, there's a one-two punch coming at the end for my anger.
那是，最后会有连环两击来展现我的愤怒。

1322
00:53:46.130 --> 00:53:46.830
But yeah.
但确实是这样。

1323
00:53:47.010 --> 00:53:47.470
All right.
好吧。

1324
00:53:47.570 --> 00:53:50.910
So people are making trades, and feelings are getting hurt.
大家都在交换礼物，感情也受到了伤害。

1325
00:53:51.110 --> 00:53:51.390
Yeah.
是啊。

1326
00:53:51.890 --> 00:53:55.130
And Pam does not go back and get the teapot.
而且帕姆没有回去拿那个茶壶。

1327
00:53:55.310 --> 00:53:56.230
She gets the iPod.
她拿了iPod。

1328
00:53:56.370 --> 00:53:56.910
She does.
她确实拿了。

1329
00:53:57.050 --> 00:54:02.570
When it's Pam's turn to pick again, she picks the iPod instead of the teapot, and Jim is
当轮到帕姆再次挑选时，她选了iPod而不是茶壶，吉姆

1330
00:54:02.570 --> 00:54:03.370
so hurt.
非常受伤。

1331
00:54:03.610 --> 00:54:04.390
He's so hurt.
他太受伤了。

1332
00:54:04.530 --> 00:54:07.170
And I, you know, I watched this, and I was like, come on, Pam.
我，你知道，我看着这一幕，心想，拜托，帕姆。

1333
00:54:07.310 --> 00:54:11.490
But then, you know, Pam doesn't know what all is in the teapot.
但后来，你知道，帕姆不知道茶壶里到底有什么。

1334
00:54:11.610 --> 00:54:12.150
She doesn't.
她不知道。

1335
00:54:12.270 --> 00:54:13.950
And that's what sort of justified it for me.
这就是为什么我觉得这在某种程度上是可以原谅的。

1336
00:54:14.030 --> 00:54:15.450
She's just like, this is an iPod.
她只是觉得，这是个iPod。

1337
00:54:15.450 --> 00:54:22.290
This iPod has completely hijacked this whole fun party and gift exchange, because everybody
这个iPod彻底劫持了整个有趣的派对和礼物交换，因为每个

1338
00:54:22.290 --> 00:54:25.690
who's sitting in this seat is just thinking about trying to get this iPod.
坐在座位上的人都在想着怎么得到这个iPod。

1339
00:54:25.810 --> 00:54:26.990
And so is Pam.
帕姆也是。

1340
00:54:27.390 --> 00:54:30.770
Unfortunately, I think she kind of forgot about the teapot.
不幸的是，我觉得她有点忘了茶壶的事。

1341
00:54:30.870 --> 00:54:31.930
So it was her time to pick.
所以轮到她选的时候。

1342
00:54:32.050 --> 00:54:32.970
She was just like, iPod.
她就直接选了iPod。

1343
00:54:33.090 --> 00:54:35.190
But she also doesn't know what's in the teapot.
但她也不知道茶壶里装的是什么。

1344
00:54:35.290 --> 00:54:35.710
She doesn't.
她不知道。

1345
00:54:35.710 --> 00:54:37.450
She doesn't know how high the stakes are for Jim.
她不知道这对吉姆来说赌注有多大。

1346
00:54:37.610 --> 00:54:37.670
No.
不知道。

1347
00:54:37.810 --> 00:54:38.310
She doesn't.
她确实不知道。

1348
00:54:38.370 --> 00:54:40.550
I think it's kind of an innocent moment, honestly.
老实说，我觉得这算是一个无心的时刻。

1349
00:54:45.810 --> 00:54:48.210
I mean, Ryan gets a placard that says Kelly.
我是说，瑞安拿到了一个写着凯莉名字的牌子。

1350
00:54:48.410 --> 00:54:50.970
He gets like, you know, a desk, whatever, nameplate.
他拿到了一个，你知道，桌子上的那种名牌。

1351
00:54:51.190 --> 00:54:51.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1352
00:54:51.390 --> 00:54:54.930
Like, these were not meant to be Yankee Swap gifts.
这些本来就不是打算拿来玩“洋基交换”礼物的。

1353
00:54:55.050 --> 00:54:55.610
They were not.
确实不是。

1354
00:54:55.870 --> 00:54:57.390
They were meant for certain people.
它们是给特定的人准备的。

1355
00:54:58.390 --> 00:55:04.150
Well, at this point, the party has completely broken down, and Michael goes to the liquor
好吧，此时派对已经彻底乱套了，迈克尔去了酒类

1356
00:55:04.150 --> 00:55:04.570
store.
商店。

1357
00:55:04.750 --> 00:55:06.370
Now, I want to point out a few things.
现在，我想指出几点。

1358
00:55:06.450 --> 00:55:11.450
I know what you're going to point out, because, lady, I have the DVDs now.
我知道你要指出什么，因为女士，我现在有DVD了。

1359
00:55:11.770 --> 00:55:12.590
So, go.
所以，说吧。

1360
00:55:12.710 --> 00:55:13.090
Do it.
开始吧。

1361
00:55:13.230 --> 00:55:14.290
Do you know what I'm going to say?
你知道我要说什么吗？

1362
00:55:14.290 --> 00:55:16.670
Is it about the attendant at the liquor store?
是关于酒类商店的那个店员吗？

1363
00:55:16.890 --> 00:55:20.650
I have one thing to say about him, but I just thought I wanted to point out that it's
关于他我确实有一点要说，但我只是想指出，酒类商店的窗外

1364
00:55:20.650 --> 00:55:23.730
also snowing outside the window of the liquor store.
也在下雪。

1365
00:55:24.070 --> 00:55:24.270
Yeah.
没错。

1366
00:55:24.510 --> 00:55:25.850
They made it snow there, too.
他们在那儿也制造了下雪的效果。

1367
00:55:26.110 --> 00:55:26.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

1368
00:55:26.870 --> 00:55:27.450
Nice detail.
不错的细节。

1369
00:55:27.630 --> 00:55:28.110
Nice touch.
点睛之笔。

1370
00:55:28.330 --> 00:55:28.910
Good continuity.
连贯性做得很好。

1371
00:55:29.130 --> 00:55:29.750
Veda was on it.
维达很细心。

1372
00:55:29.970 --> 00:55:35.130
Well, I read that our writers found out in Pennsylvania that if you work at a liquor
我读到过，我们的编剧在宾夕法尼亚州了解到，如果你在酒类

1373
00:55:35.130 --> 00:55:36.330
store, you have to wear a tie.
商店工作，你就必须打领带。

1374
00:55:36.510 --> 00:55:36.890
Yes.
是的。

1375
00:55:37.130 --> 00:55:41.790
And so, that was part of this character description, is that he had to have on a tie.
所以，这是角色设定的一部分，他必须戴着领带。

1376
00:55:41.990 --> 00:55:42.590
Isn't that great?
这不是很棒吗？

1377
00:55:42.590 --> 00:55:46.810
And I thought the actor, his name is Ryan Martin, did a fantastic job.
我觉得那位演员，他叫瑞安·马丁，表现得非常出色。

1378
00:55:46.990 --> 00:55:47.070
So good.
太棒了。

1379
00:55:47.070 --> 00:55:49.690
He just really, like, takes in all of that vodka.
他真的，就像是，把那些伏特加全买下了。

1380
00:55:50.530 --> 00:55:51.390
Fifteen bottles.
十五瓶。

1381
00:55:51.450 --> 00:55:52.210
Fifteen bottles.
十五瓶。

1382
00:55:53.350 --> 00:55:53.870
Craziness.
太疯狂了。

1383
00:55:54.430 --> 00:55:54.850
Okay.
好的。

1384
00:55:54.850 --> 00:55:56.510
So, then we go back to the party.
然后我们回到派对。

1385
00:55:56.810 --> 00:56:02.030
Michael brings all this vodka back into the party, and at 16, 10 minutes, this is the
迈克尔把这些伏特加带回了派对，在16分10秒处，这是

1386
00:56:02.030 --> 00:56:05.390
next phase of Angela's spiral.
安吉拉崩溃的下一个阶段。

1387
00:56:05.510 --> 00:56:06.290
Oh, say it.
哦，说出来吧。

1388
00:56:06.330 --> 00:56:07.870
So, Michael has vodka.
所以，迈克尔带了伏特加。

1389
00:56:07.970 --> 00:56:09.570
And she's like, what are you doing?
然后她说，你在干什么？

1390
00:56:10.090 --> 00:56:12.110
There's no alcohol at the party.
派对上没有酒精饮料。

1391
00:56:12.110 --> 00:56:15.430
You know, Angela speaks up, and Toby speaks up.
你知道，安吉拉站出来说话了，托比也站出来说话了。

1392
00:56:15.650 --> 00:56:16.550
No one else cares.
其他人都不在乎。

1393
00:56:17.270 --> 00:56:18.110
But now she's like-
但现在她就像是——

1394
00:56:18.110 --> 00:56:18.750
Toby speaks up?
托比站出来说话了？

1395
00:56:18.790 --> 00:56:19.330
I miss that.
我错过了那个细节。

1396
00:56:19.490 --> 00:56:19.670
Yeah.
是的。

1397
00:56:19.850 --> 00:56:22.490
Toby's like, Michael, we really shouldn't have it.
托比说，迈克尔，我们真的不该喝这个。

1398
00:56:22.530 --> 00:56:23.930
And he goes, just shut it, Toby.
然后他说，闭嘴吧，托比。

1399
00:56:24.130 --> 00:56:24.850
It's a party.
这是派对。

1400
00:56:25.070 --> 00:56:28.910
But then later, I feel like Toby brings Todd Packer a drink.
但后来，我觉得托比好像给托德·帕克递了一杯酒。

1401
00:56:29.130 --> 00:56:29.750
Well, no.
嗯，不是。

1402
00:56:29.870 --> 00:56:30.330
It's all-
这完全是——

1403
00:56:30.890 --> 00:56:32.690
All bets are off at this point.
现在一切都难说了。

1404
00:56:32.970 --> 00:56:38.610
And, you know, you have to remember that Michael told the party planning committee that he wanted
而且，你知道，你得记住迈克尔告诉派对策划委员会，他希望

1405
00:56:38.610 --> 00:56:42.690
this Christmas party to be like, and I quote, a Playboy Mansion party.
这次圣诞派对要像，引用他的话，花花公子豪宅派对那样。

1406
00:56:42.930 --> 00:56:43.130
Yeah.
是啊。

1407
00:56:43.390 --> 00:56:44.370
That was his hope.
那是他的愿望。

1408
00:56:44.430 --> 00:56:44.930
That's his goal.
那是他的目标。

1409
00:56:45.090 --> 00:56:45.930
That's his goal.
那是他的目标。

1410
00:56:46.170 --> 00:56:49.590
So, but yeah, Angela is now super ticked, because now there's alcohol.
所以，没错，安吉拉现在超级生气，因为现在有酒了。

1411
00:56:50.030 --> 00:56:52.370
I'm surprised her whole head didn't explode.
我很惊讶她的头居然没炸开。

1412
00:56:52.550 --> 00:56:56.450
Well, it's about to, because the next two are what set it into motion.
嗯，快要炸了，因为接下来的两件事让事态进一步升级。

1413
00:56:56.450 --> 00:56:56.990
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1414
00:56:56.990 --> 00:57:02.350
Well, now we have the scene where Jim is trying to get the teapot back from Dwight.
好了，现在我们看到吉姆试图从德怀特那里拿回茶壶的场景。

1415
00:57:02.570 --> 00:57:07.050
Jim offers to trade him the shamrock keychain, and he says, come on, it'll be good luck.
吉姆提出用三叶草钥匙扣跟他换，他说，来吧，这会带来好运的。

1416
00:57:07.150 --> 00:57:11.390
And that's when Dwight has his line, a real man makes his own luck.
就在那时，德怀特说了那句台词：真正的男人会创造自己的运气。

1417
00:57:11.590 --> 00:57:20.230
Billy Zane, Titanic, and Angela, you made the entire cast t-shirts with that quote on them,
比利·赞恩，《泰坦尼克号》，安吉拉，你给整个剧组做了印有那句台词的T恤，

1418
00:57:20.270 --> 00:57:21.730
and I still have mine.
我到现在还留着我的那件。

1419
00:57:21.810 --> 00:57:22.970
Oh, my gosh, you do?
天哪，你真的留着？

1420
00:57:23.050 --> 00:57:23.490
I do.
我留着。

1421
00:57:23.590 --> 00:57:25.290
It's a gray, long-sleeved t-shirt.
那是一件灰色的长袖T恤。

1422
00:57:25.410 --> 00:57:26.650
Yes, with black writing.
是的，上面有黑色的字。

1423
00:57:26.650 --> 00:57:28.310
Just a quote across it.
上面就印着那句引语。

1424
00:57:28.370 --> 00:57:34.210
Yeah, so I had a friend at the time who had a t-shirt press, because she had a small business,
是啊，当时我有个朋友有台T恤印刷机，因为她开了家小店，

1425
00:57:34.790 --> 00:57:37.550
and I loved this line so much.
我太喜欢这句台词了。

1426
00:57:37.550 --> 00:57:41.330
I thought it was hilarious of all people for Dwight to quote.
我觉得德怀特引用这句话简直太搞笑了。

1427
00:57:41.490 --> 00:57:42.750
It would be Billy Zane.
竟然会是比利·赞恩。

1428
00:57:43.010 --> 00:57:45.390
Well, people were asking if we gave each other gifts.
嗯，有人问我们是否互赠了礼物。

1429
00:57:45.490 --> 00:57:46.130
That was a gift.
那就算是一份礼物。

1430
00:57:46.210 --> 00:57:46.750
You gave that out.
你把那个送出去了。

1431
00:57:46.810 --> 00:57:48.850
I think you actually gave that out at Christmas that year.
我想你那年圣诞节确实把那个送给大家了。

1432
00:57:48.950 --> 00:57:50.690
I did, and you gave everyone an ornament.
我送了，而你送了每个人一个装饰品。

1433
00:57:50.970 --> 00:57:55.110
Yes, I got that cast photo, and I had it printed on an ornament for everyone.
是的，我拿到了那张剧组照，然后把它印在装饰品上送给了大家。

1434
00:57:55.310 --> 00:57:55.570
Yep.
没错。

1435
00:57:56.650 --> 00:58:02.850
The idea that Dwight wants to keep the teapot in order to wash out his nasal passages with
德怀特想留着茶壶是为了用绿茶清洗鼻腔，这个点子是基于格雷格·丹尼尔斯

1436
00:58:02.850 --> 00:58:06.030
green tea is based on something that Greg Daniels has actually done.
真的做过的事情。

1437
00:58:06.370 --> 00:58:07.730
Like with a neti pot?
就像用洗鼻壶那样？

1438
00:58:08.110 --> 00:58:11.730
Yeah, I mean, but I've never put green tea in a neti pot.
是啊，我是说，但我从来没在洗鼻壶里放过绿茶。

1439
00:58:11.970 --> 00:58:13.090
I haven't either.
我也没放过。

1440
00:58:13.090 --> 00:58:15.670
I've only used the saline solution that is recommended.
我只用过推荐的生理盐水。

1441
00:58:15.670 --> 00:58:25.030
But I could see Greg reading about it and giving it a try, but Rain, the way Rain was in that
但我能想象格雷格读到这个方法后去尝试了一下，但是雷恩，雷恩在那个场景里的样子，

1442
00:58:25.030 --> 00:58:29.330
scene, and then he shoved that teapot into his nostril.
然后他把那个茶壶塞进了鼻孔里。

1443
00:58:29.490 --> 00:58:29.830
Yeah.
是啊。

1444
00:58:29.830 --> 00:58:34.270
And just John's face as Jim is just like, are you kidding me?
还有约翰饰演的吉姆那副表情，简直就像在说，你在开玩笑吗？

1445
00:58:34.610 --> 00:58:37.130
That, that's who gets my teapot?
这就是拿到我茶壶的人？

1446
00:58:37.370 --> 00:58:38.630
Like, it's so perfect.
真的太完美了。

1447
00:58:38.630 --> 00:58:39.930
He's so bummed.
他太沮丧了。

1448
00:58:40.150 --> 00:58:47.830
Now, when I watched this with Lee, Lee said he wondered how Dwight didn't find the note in the box
现在，当我和李一起看这一集时，李说他很纳闷德怀特怎么没发现盒子里的小纸条，

1449
00:58:48.890 --> 00:58:52.070
or how Dwight didn't open up the teapot.
或者德怀特怎么没打开茶壶看看。

1450
00:58:52.250 --> 00:58:53.450
I thought of all of those things.
这些问题我也都想过。

1451
00:58:53.670 --> 00:58:57.390
I thought Dwight now has the cassette and the sauce packet.
我以为德怀特现在拿到了磁带和酱料包。

1452
00:58:57.390 --> 00:59:03.110
But, I mean, so you have to sort of suspend belief, I guess, at that moment that, that
但是，我是说，你得在那一刻稍微放下逻辑，我想，就是那个……

1453
00:59:03.110 --> 00:59:05.810
he took those out and just shoved them aside, like, hmm, what's this crap?
他把那些东西拿出来，随手扔到一边，心想，嗯，这是什么垃圾？

1454
00:59:05.990 --> 00:59:07.610
And just sort of shoved them aside in the box.
就那样随手扔在盒子里。

1455
00:59:07.910 --> 00:59:11.290
Well, also, I don't think Jim is trying to get the teapot back for Pam.
嗯，还有，我不觉得吉姆是为了帕姆才想把茶壶拿回来的。

1456
00:59:11.510 --> 00:59:14.250
I think he's just trying to get the teapot back for himself.
我觉得他只是想把茶壶拿回来给自己。

1457
00:59:14.390 --> 00:59:15.570
He's just going to keep it now.
他现在打算把它留下了。

1458
00:59:15.850 --> 00:59:17.410
That's what I think the motivation is there.
我觉得他的动机就是这样。

1459
00:59:17.550 --> 00:59:22.910
Because Pam is over, you know, up at the desk with Roy looking through her new iPod.
因为帕姆在那边，你知道，在前台和罗伊一起看她那台新iPod。

1460
00:59:23.030 --> 00:59:26.150
I think Jim just wants to get it back because I think there's things inside it that
我觉得吉姆只是想拿回来，因为我觉得里面有些东西……

1461
00:59:27.390 --> 00:59:27.590
Exactly.
没错。

1462
00:59:27.850 --> 00:59:31.130
But he's going to trade the keychain and he's just going to take that teapot home now.
但他会用钥匙扣去交换，然后他现在打算把那个茶壶带回家。

1463
00:59:31.310 --> 00:59:35.050
So Pam is up at reception and she's showing Roy her new iPod.
所以帕姆在前台，正在给罗伊看她的新iPod。

1464
00:59:35.170 --> 00:59:36.070
He's now at the party.
他现在在派对上了。

1465
00:59:36.190 --> 00:59:37.470
He wasn't there for Yankee Swap.
他没参加之前的“洋基交换”礼物活动。

1466
00:59:37.630 --> 00:59:41.610
But he's all excited because now he doesn't have to buy it for Pam for Christmas.
但他很兴奋，因为现在他不用给帕姆买圣诞礼物了。

1467
00:59:41.910 --> 00:59:44.330
He was going to buy her this iPod, he tells her.
他告诉她，他本来打算给她买这台iPod的。

1468
00:59:44.490 --> 00:59:47.070
And now he doesn't have to or he's just going to get her a sweater.
现在他不用买了，或者他打算只给她买件毛衣。

1469
00:59:47.610 --> 00:59:48.270
Thanks, Roy.
谢了，罗伊。

1470
00:59:48.530 --> 00:59:51.970
Now the party is like 15 bottles of vodka in.
现在派对已经喝掉了大概15瓶伏特加。

1471
00:59:52.090 --> 00:59:53.590
Todd Packer has showed up.
托德·帕克出现了。

1472
00:59:53.610 --> 00:59:54.090
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

1473
00:59:54.250 --> 00:59:55.290
It's getting crazy.
场面开始失控了。

1474
00:59:55.290 --> 00:59:57.570
And everyone's doing shots.
大家都在喝烈酒。

1475
00:59:57.730 --> 00:59:58.510
Angela's fuming.
安吉拉气坏了。

1476
00:59:58.810 --> 00:59:59.510
I am fuming.
我气炸了。

1477
00:59:59.530 --> 01:00:03.710
But the icing on the cake of my pissed offness is about to happen.
但我愤怒情绪的巅峰时刻即将到来。

1478
01:00:04.010 --> 01:00:05.250
Oh, say it.
噢，说出来吧。

1479
01:00:05.530 --> 01:00:08.970
Michael shouts to the whole bullpen.
迈克尔对着整个办公区大喊。

1480
01:00:08.970 --> 01:00:11.250
He says, oh, my gosh.
他说，噢，天哪。

1481
01:00:11.410 --> 01:00:13.730
Yes, Ryan, the king of the party planning.
没错，瑞安，派对策划之王。

1482
01:00:14.330 --> 01:00:15.650
Oh, thank you.
噢，谢谢。

1483
01:00:15.770 --> 01:00:18.350
Thank you to Ryan for this awesome party.
感谢瑞安举办了这场精彩的派对。

1484
01:00:18.350 --> 01:00:22.250
And the camera pans to me and I am livid.
镜头转向我，我当时火冒三丈。

1485
01:00:23.230 --> 01:00:27.330
Ryan, the temp, the king of the party planning committee.
瑞安，那个临时工，派对策划委员会之王。

1486
01:00:27.510 --> 01:00:28.470
Are you kidding me?
你在开玩笑吗？

1487
01:00:28.910 --> 01:00:30.630
Oh, that's it.
噢，够了。

1488
01:00:30.770 --> 01:00:32.390
She is pissed.
她气疯了。

1489
01:00:32.690 --> 01:00:33.530
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1490
01:00:33.970 --> 01:00:35.950
And it's only going to get worse.
而且情况只会变得更糟。

1491
01:00:36.270 --> 01:00:39.490
That's not even still the worst thing that's happened to Angela.
这甚至还不是安吉拉在这集里遇到的最糟糕的事。

1492
01:00:39.730 --> 01:00:39.990
Nope.
没错。

1493
01:00:40.090 --> 01:00:42.330
I had a headache by the end of this episode.
这一集结束时我头都疼了。

1494
01:00:42.330 --> 01:00:43.090
You must have.
你肯定头疼。

1495
01:00:43.130 --> 01:00:47.530
You were just scowling and pushing anger out of your temples this whole episode.
你整集都在皱着眉头，太阳穴都在往外冒火。

1496
01:00:48.790 --> 01:00:53.250
You know when Todd Packer shows up and he has that line, what's up, my nerds?
你知道托德·帕克出现时说的那句台词吗，“嘿，我的书呆子们？”

1497
01:00:53.350 --> 01:00:54.450
My nerds.
“我的书呆子们”。

1498
01:00:54.530 --> 01:00:56.570
That was an improv, sort of.
那算是即兴发挥。

1499
01:00:56.770 --> 01:01:00.330
In the script, what was written was, what's up, nerds?
剧本里写的是，“嘿，书呆子们？”

1500
01:01:01.530 --> 01:01:06.550
And he just gave it that extra special touch of, what's up, my nerds?
他只是加了那个特别的润色，变成了“嘿，我的书呆子们？”

1501
01:01:06.550 --> 01:01:06.910
I know.
我知道。

1502
01:01:07.050 --> 01:01:08.250
Well, that's also Dave Koechner.
嗯，那也是戴夫·科克纳。

1503
01:01:08.430 --> 01:01:12.290
I mean, I think even the line when he's like, Packer, need a drinky.
我是说，我觉得甚至连他说“帕克，来杯喝的”那句台词时，

1504
01:01:12.490 --> 01:01:12.670
Yeah.
没错。

1505
01:01:13.330 --> 01:01:15.730
The line was probably like, he was getting me a drink.
那句台词大概就是，他当时在给我拿饮料。

1506
01:01:15.870 --> 01:01:16.030
Yeah.
是啊。

1507
01:01:16.270 --> 01:01:16.610
You know?
你懂吧？

1508
01:01:17.470 --> 01:01:19.370
He brought so much to that role.
他为那个角色注入了太多东西。

1509
01:01:19.510 --> 01:01:20.050
It was amazing.
太棒了。

1510
01:01:20.170 --> 01:01:23.530
And well, you know when he has to lay down on the desk and get the silly string on him,
还有，你知道当他必须躺在桌子上，身上被喷满彩带的时候，

1511
01:01:23.570 --> 01:01:24.470
like when he passes out?
就是他喝醉昏过去的时候？

1512
01:01:24.670 --> 01:01:25.750
I remember shooting that.
我还记得拍那场戏的情景。

1513
01:01:25.870 --> 01:01:27.410
He had to lay there forever.
他得在那儿躺好久。

1514
01:01:27.610 --> 01:01:30.930
So he laid down on those desks, which were not comfortable, right?
他躺在那些桌子上，那可一点都不舒服，对吧？

1515
01:01:31.050 --> 01:01:32.630
And then they silly stringed his head.
然后他们往他头上喷彩带。

1516
01:01:33.050 --> 01:01:36.250
And then we had all these scenes where that's what he's doing.
之后我们拍的所有场景他都得保持那个样子。

1517
01:01:36.550 --> 01:01:40.830
Well, if he got up, all the stuff that he was decorated in would have fallen off.
嗯，如果他站起来，他身上那些装饰物就全掉光了。

1518
01:01:40.910 --> 01:01:42.670
It would have been impossible to recreate.
那样就没法还原现场了。

1519
01:01:42.670 --> 01:01:46.030
So he had to just lay there, even when we were on a break.
所以即使是在休息的时候，他也必须躺在那儿。

1520
01:01:46.230 --> 01:01:47.490
Even when we were on a break.
即使是在休息的时候。

1521
01:01:47.630 --> 01:01:48.870
And he was such a trooper.
他真是个硬汉。

1522
01:01:49.010 --> 01:01:49.690
Talk about a trooper.
说到硬汉。

1523
01:01:49.890 --> 01:01:56.050
And I wrote in my MySpace blog that Kate and I, because Kate and I knew Dave from Improv Days.
我在我的MySpace博客里写过，凯特和我，因为我和凯特在即兴表演时期就认识戴夫了。

1524
01:01:56.110 --> 01:01:58.190
We had all done improv shows together.
我们以前一起做过即兴表演秀。

1525
01:01:58.430 --> 01:02:02.470
That Kate and I walked over and talked to him while he had to lay on his back.
凯特和我走过去，趁他不得不躺着的时候和他聊天。

1526
01:02:02.750 --> 01:02:05.930
And we just sort of caught up and that it was so fun to see him.
我们只是叙了叙旧，能见到他真是太开心了。

1527
01:02:05.930 --> 01:02:13.530
But I want you guys to know, if you're wondering what Todd Packer looks like at 20 minutes, 19 seconds, to really paint a picture here.
但我得让你们知道，如果你们好奇托德·帕克在20分19秒时是什么样子，我来给你们描绘一下画面。

1528
01:02:13.610 --> 01:02:13.830
Yeah.
没错。

1529
01:02:13.970 --> 01:02:19.610
He's laying on his back kind of across a desk area partition right in the middle of the room.
他仰面躺在房间中央办公桌区域的隔板上。

1530
01:02:19.790 --> 01:02:27.490
He has blue silly string on his head, Christmas lights around his torso, Christmas garland around his torso,
他头上喷着蓝色彩带，躯干上缠着圣诞彩灯和圣诞花环，

1531
01:02:28.150 --> 01:02:37.430
Dwight's desk nameplate on his stomach, and there's like a red empty solo cup kind of just like in his, like the crook of his arm.
肚子上放着德怀特的桌牌，手臂弯处还夹着一个红色的空塑料杯。

1532
01:02:37.770 --> 01:02:41.650
And he had to lay like that with all those things on top of him.
他必须带着所有这些东西保持那个姿势躺着。

1533
01:02:41.790 --> 01:02:44.410
He passes out so quickly.
他昏睡得太快了。

1534
01:02:44.670 --> 01:02:47.990
You have to imagine he showed up already half drunk.
你得想象他到场时就已经半醉了。

1535
01:02:48.190 --> 01:02:49.110
You know he did.
你知道他肯定是。

1536
01:02:49.110 --> 01:02:49.870
You know he did.
你知道他肯定是。

1537
01:02:49.870 --> 01:02:50.790
You know he did.
你知道他肯定是。

1538
01:02:51.030 --> 01:02:51.990
Okay, guys.
好了，各位。

1539
01:02:52.170 --> 01:02:58.910
So now we have the scene where Pam reveals to Jim that she got her teapot back.
现在到了帕姆向吉姆透露她拿回茶壶的那场戏。

1540
01:02:59.590 --> 01:03:06.430
She trades Dwight the iPod for the teapot, and now she's going to look inside and find all the iteMs.
她用iPod跟德怀特换回了茶壶，现在她要往里看，找出里面的所有物品。

1541
01:03:06.450 --> 01:03:09.610
And it's very charming and sweet, and she is so delighted.
那场戏非常迷人且甜蜜，她看起来特别高兴。

1542
01:03:09.830 --> 01:03:15.270
But in this moment, Jim secretly steals the note back and puts it in his pocket.
但在那一刻，吉姆偷偷把纸条拿了回来，放进了自己的口袋。

1543
01:03:15.510 --> 01:03:16.150
I know.
我知道。

1544
01:03:16.150 --> 01:03:17.670
He lost his courage.
他失去了勇气。

1545
01:03:17.670 --> 01:03:18.470
He did.
确实。

1546
01:03:18.910 --> 01:03:25.930
Now, when we reached out to fans to ask them what they wanted to know about the Christmas episode,
现在，当我们联系粉丝询问他们想了解关于圣诞特辑的什么内容时，

1547
01:03:26.470 --> 01:03:33.470
I would say that about 80% of the comments and emails we received were along the lines of,
我想说，我们收到的评论和邮件中大约80%都是在问，

1548
01:03:33.810 --> 01:03:35.650
what is in the teapot note?
茶壶里的纸条写了什么？

1549
01:03:36.050 --> 01:03:39.450
Because as you know, in this episode, Pam does not read it.
因为如你们所知，在这一集中，帕姆并没有读它。

1550
01:03:39.570 --> 01:03:40.490
It is not revealed.
内容没有揭晓。

1551
01:03:40.490 --> 01:03:49.150
But then, in season nine, there's a scene where Jim has the documentary film crew put together footage of their romance,
但后来在第九季，有一个场景是吉姆让纪录片摄制组把他们恋爱的片段剪辑在一起，

1552
01:03:49.150 --> 01:03:55.110
and he shows it to Pam, and Pam sees that there was a note that Jim steals back,
他给帕姆看，帕姆发现有一张纸条是吉姆偷偷拿回来的，

1553
01:03:55.290 --> 01:03:58.650
and then he hands it to her, and she reads it.
然后他把纸条递给她，她读了上面的内容。

1554
01:03:58.790 --> 01:03:59.970
How brilliant is that?
这太绝了，不是吗？

1555
01:04:00.070 --> 01:04:01.050
And you know who that is?
你知道那是谁的手笔吗？

1556
01:04:01.110 --> 01:04:02.090
That's Greg Daniels.
那是格雷格·丹尼尔斯。

1557
01:04:02.170 --> 01:04:02.330
Yeah.
没错。

1558
01:04:02.330 --> 01:04:06.750
Because he was such a master at beautiful callback moments.
因为他非常擅长这种精妙的呼应时刻。

1559
01:04:07.370 --> 01:04:08.510
I love that.
我太喜欢那个了。

1560
01:04:08.650 --> 01:04:12.330
Well, from the time that Jim stole the note, it drove people crazy.
嗯，从吉姆偷走那张纸条开始，它就让观众们抓心挠肝的。

1561
01:04:12.630 --> 01:04:15.890
They always wanted to know what had been written in the note.
大家一直想知道纸条上写了什么。

1562
01:04:16.050 --> 01:04:17.550
Would Pam ever get the note?
帕姆到底能不能看到那张纸条？

1563
01:04:17.710 --> 01:04:20.410
For years and years, will he ever give her the note?
好多年过去了，他到底会不会把纸条给她？

1564
01:04:20.650 --> 01:04:24.170
Around the time of the wedding, people wanted him to give it to her as a wedding gift.
在婚礼前后，大家都希望他能把纸条当作结婚礼物送给她。

1565
01:04:24.830 --> 01:04:26.450
Greg saved it till the end.
但格雷格把它留到了最后。

1566
01:04:26.450 --> 01:04:32.230
And if I'm going to say something that I've never said before, I also feel like I'm maybe going to cry.
如果我要说一件我从未公开过的事，我觉得我可能要哭了。

1567
01:04:32.690 --> 01:04:33.190
What?
什么？

1568
01:04:33.450 --> 01:04:33.910
Wait.
等等。

1569
01:04:34.390 --> 01:04:34.910
Wait.
等等。

1570
01:04:35.210 --> 01:04:35.590
What?
什么？

1571
01:04:36.250 --> 01:04:39.150
Are you going to say what was in the note?
你是要说纸条上写了什么吗？

1572
01:04:39.670 --> 01:04:41.350
Are you going to say what was in the note?
你是要说纸条上写了什么吗？

1573
01:04:42.630 --> 01:04:43.430
Sort of.
算是吧。

1574
01:04:43.890 --> 01:04:46.410
Because I don't know what was on that card.
因为我也不知道那张卡片上写了什么。

1575
01:04:46.630 --> 01:04:47.490
None of us do.
我们谁都不知道。

1576
01:04:47.950 --> 01:04:50.470
I'm the only one who knows, and John knows.
只有我知道，还有约翰知道。

1577
01:04:50.910 --> 01:04:52.470
Oh my gosh, lady.
天哪，女士。

1578
01:04:52.470 --> 01:05:10.910
In that episode in Season 9, I believe Greg suggested to John that he write a personal message from himself to me, just saying what our time together on The Office meant to him.
在第九季的那一集里，我想是格雷格建议约翰写一段他自己想对我说的话，就写我们一起拍摄《办公室》对他意味着什么。

1579
01:05:11.030 --> 01:05:11.770
Oh, Jenna.
噢，珍娜。

1580
01:05:13.170 --> 01:05:14.810
Because we were wrapping up filming.
因为当时我们快要结束拍摄了。

1581
01:05:14.810 --> 01:05:18.770
We were wrapping up the series, and we were all so emotional at that time, you know?
我们正在收尾整部剧，那时候大家都特别感伤，你知道吗？

1582
01:05:19.090 --> 01:05:22.370
We were all sort of saying goodbye in different ways.
我们都在以各自的方式告别。

1583
01:05:22.430 --> 01:05:22.870
We were.
确实是。

1584
01:05:22.870 --> 01:05:26.170
And so that was his goodbye.
所以那就是他的告别。

1585
01:05:27.290 --> 01:05:38.590
Very similar to when we filmed that scene with Steve, where I said goodbye to him at the airport, and Paul Feig told me, just run up and say goodbye to your friend Steve.
这和我们拍史蒂夫那场戏很像，我在机场和他告别，保罗·费格当时对我说，就跑过去和你朋友史蒂夫告别吧。

1586
01:05:39.350 --> 01:05:46.430
Jeff Blitz said the same thing to me when I was in the car with Oscar, and I say I love Dwight.
杰夫·布里茨在我和奥斯卡坐在车里，我说我爱德怀特的时候，也对我说了同样的话。

1587
01:05:46.970 --> 01:05:55.810
He said, Angela, in this moment, express your love for the show and everyone, and if you couldn't have it in your life anymore.
他说，安吉拉，在这一刻，表达你对这部剧和所有人的爱，就当这是你生命中最后一次拥有他们。

1588
01:05:56.870 --> 01:05:58.290
And I disintegrated.
然后我就崩溃了。

1589
01:05:58.550 --> 01:05:58.710
Yeah.
没错。

1590
01:05:59.630 --> 01:06:06.790
So I'm on camera, and I open up this note that John's written me, and I just start crying.
所以我当时在镜头前，打开了约翰写给我的那张纸条，然后就开始哭。

1591
01:06:07.050 --> 01:06:08.230
I just start bawling.
我直接泪崩了。

1592
01:06:08.490 --> 01:06:10.590
It probably, the first take was probably not usable.
第一条拍摄的素材可能根本没法用。

1593
01:06:12.970 --> 01:06:14.410
It was the sweetest note.
那是一张最贴心的纸条。

1594
01:06:14.610 --> 01:06:21.650
And you know, on camera, Pam says, I'll never say what it said, but just know it was perfect.
你知道，在镜头里，帕姆说，我永远不会说出上面写了什么，但只要知道它是完美的就行了。

1595
01:06:22.970 --> 01:06:28.310
Well, I'll never say exactly what John wrote, but I will say just know it was perfect.
嗯，我也永远不会说出约翰具体写了什么，但我会说，只要知道它是完美的就行了。

1596
01:06:28.310 --> 01:06:28.530
Perfect.
完美的。

1597
01:06:29.690 --> 01:06:31.750
So that's what was in the teapot note, guys.
所以，伙计们，茶壶纸条里写的就是这些。

1598
01:06:31.930 --> 01:06:34.030
It was a note from John to me.
那是约翰写给我的纸条。

1599
01:06:34.190 --> 01:06:37.670
A personal note about what it meant to work with you on the show.
是一张关于在剧中与我共事对他意味着什么的私人纸条。

1600
01:06:37.810 --> 01:06:38.030
Yeah.
没错。

1601
01:06:38.250 --> 01:06:38.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1602
01:06:38.650 --> 01:06:40.530
About our time together on the show, and it was really sweet.
关于我们在节目中相处的时光，真的很温馨。

1603
01:06:40.730 --> 01:06:43.450
Well, that would completely wreck me.
噢，那会让我彻底崩溃的。

1604
01:06:43.790 --> 01:06:44.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1605
01:06:44.850 --> 01:06:46.250
Oh, I love that.
噢，我喜欢这个。

1606
01:06:46.390 --> 01:06:47.350
I didn't know that.
我之前不知道。

1607
01:06:47.450 --> 01:06:48.010
Are you okay?
你还好吗？

1608
01:06:48.390 --> 01:06:48.830
Yeah.
我没事。

1609
01:06:49.050 --> 01:06:49.490
Well, crap.
好吧，真糟糕。

1610
01:06:49.490 --> 01:06:50.950
How do we talk about anything else?
我们还能聊点别的吗？

1611
01:06:50.950 --> 01:06:52.130
That was so beautiful.
那太美好了。

1612
01:06:52.670 --> 01:06:52.990
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1613
01:06:53.270 --> 01:06:54.350
That was so beautiful.
那太美好了。

1614
01:06:54.350 --> 01:06:57.230
I love that that was the direction that Greg gave.
我很喜欢格雷格给出的那个指导方向。

1615
01:06:57.230 --> 01:07:02.310
Those moments became very honest for us under that kind of direction.
在那种指导下，那些时刻对我们来说变得非常真实。

1616
01:07:03.230 --> 01:07:05.470
And we all had little moments like that.
我们每个人都有过那样的小瞬间。

1617
01:07:05.610 --> 01:07:06.810
That's a really big one, though.
不过，那确实是一个非常重大的时刻。

1618
01:07:06.990 --> 01:07:09.710
Well, there were those moments on the show that were surprises.
嗯，节目中确实有一些出人意料的时刻。

1619
01:07:10.210 --> 01:07:10.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1620
01:07:10.570 --> 01:07:16.230
Steve didn't know I was going to run up and tell him that basically that same thing.
史蒂夫不知道我会跑过去告诉他基本相同的话。

1621
01:07:17.050 --> 01:07:18.430
Steve, I'm going to miss you.
史蒂夫，我会想念你的。

1622
01:07:18.570 --> 01:07:20.130
You know, all the things that I said to him.
你知道，就是我对他说过的那些话。

1623
01:07:20.450 --> 01:07:22.710
Oscar didn't know the note that Jeff Blitz gave me.
奥斯卡不知道杰夫·布里茨给我的那张纸条。

1624
01:07:22.810 --> 01:07:22.950
Yeah.
是啊。

1625
01:07:22.950 --> 01:07:28.550
So when all that emotion came, it was very, like, completely out of nowhere for him.
所以当那种情绪涌上来时，对他来说完全是意料之外的。

1626
01:07:28.770 --> 01:07:28.890
Yeah.
是啊。

1627
01:07:29.330 --> 01:07:29.710
Okay.
好吧。

1628
01:07:29.930 --> 01:07:31.690
Well, geez, Louise.
天哪，真是的。

1629
01:07:32.190 --> 01:07:32.850
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1630
01:07:33.010 --> 01:07:33.610
That's okay.
没关系。

1631
01:07:33.750 --> 01:07:35.430
Where are we at in this episode?
我们这一集进行到哪儿了？

1632
01:07:35.950 --> 01:07:41.070
Well, we're at the moment when Kelly approaches Dwight in the kitchen.
嗯，进行到凯莉在厨房接近德怀特的那一刻了。

1633
01:07:41.290 --> 01:07:42.430
Kelly, that hussy.
凯莉那个小妖精。

1634
01:07:42.610 --> 01:07:45.030
Oh, with her hair half down, half up.
噢，她还梳着半披半扎的发型。

1635
01:07:45.030 --> 01:07:45.830
I know.
我知道。

1636
01:07:46.030 --> 01:07:49.250
She goes up to my man and lays one on him.
她走到我男人面前，然后吻了他。

1637
01:07:49.310 --> 01:07:49.810
She does.
确实如此。

1638
01:07:50.230 --> 01:07:53.990
And Angela sees it, and that is it.
安吉拉看到了，然后一切就完了。

1639
01:07:54.350 --> 01:08:01.670
You know, a lot of people wrote in and commented that you're standing in front of a poster that says commitment.
你知道，很多人写信评论说你当时正站在一张写着“承诺”的海报前。

1640
01:08:02.090 --> 01:08:02.790
Am I really?
真的吗？

1641
01:08:02.930 --> 01:08:03.230
Yes.
是的。

1642
01:08:03.310 --> 01:08:03.790
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1643
01:08:03.790 --> 01:08:04.690
I didn't even notice.
我都没注意到。

1644
01:08:04.950 --> 01:08:06.010
That is so funny.
那太搞笑了。

1645
01:08:06.010 --> 01:08:07.950
I think I was just so focused on the scene.
我想我当时太专注于那场戏了。

1646
01:08:08.550 --> 01:08:09.030
Wow.
哇。

1647
01:08:09.450 --> 01:08:09.750
Yes.
是的。

1648
01:08:10.010 --> 01:08:11.790
Angela loses it.
安吉拉失控了。

1649
01:08:12.290 --> 01:08:13.070
Loses it.
彻底失控。

1650
01:08:13.190 --> 01:08:15.250
And this takes us outside.
然后这把我们带到了外面。

1651
01:08:15.890 --> 01:08:19.990
She's left the party, and now I have some stuff to tell you guys about this scene.
她已经离开派对，现在我有些关于这场戏的事要告诉大家。

1652
01:08:20.010 --> 01:08:20.210
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1653
01:08:20.870 --> 01:08:21.330
All right.
好吧。

1654
01:08:21.590 --> 01:08:23.090
20 minutes, 16 seconds.
20分16秒。

1655
01:08:23.530 --> 01:08:25.750
The ultimate Angela pissed-offness has happened.
安吉拉终极愤怒时刻发生了。

1656
01:08:26.330 --> 01:08:28.090
Here's some behind the scenes of this scene.
这里有一些这场戏的幕后花絮。

1657
01:08:28.690 --> 01:08:32.490
You have a guy up on the roof, and he's got the soap snow.
有个家伙在屋顶上，他拿着肥皂雪。

1658
01:08:32.730 --> 01:08:33.050
Yep.
没错。

1659
01:08:33.170 --> 01:08:33.830
That he's going to-
他打算……

1660
01:08:33.830 --> 01:08:34.710
Falling into your eyes.
掉进你的眼睛里。

1661
01:08:34.710 --> 01:08:35.310
He's going to-
他打算……

1662
01:08:35.310 --> 01:08:35.490
Yeah.
是啊。

1663
01:08:35.750 --> 01:08:36.650
It's stinging.
很刺眼。

1664
01:08:37.590 --> 01:08:41.190
And then there's snow on the ground, because they've put real snow on the ground.
然后地上有雪，因为他们往地上铺了真雪。

1665
01:08:41.530 --> 01:08:44.370
We filmed this scene at the end of the day, and everyone had gone.
我们是在一天结束时拍这场戏的，当时大家都走了。

1666
01:08:44.810 --> 01:08:48.750
It was just me and Charles McDougal, Randall Einhorn, and Mike Schur.
只剩下我和查尔斯·麦克杜格尔、兰德尔·艾因霍恩，还有迈克·舒尔。

1667
01:08:48.890 --> 01:08:50.970
So it was just a kind of a skeleton crew at this point.
所以当时只有精简的工作人员在场。

1668
01:08:51.030 --> 01:08:52.930
Those are always some of my most favorite shoots.
那总是我最喜欢的拍摄时刻之一。

1669
01:08:53.190 --> 01:08:54.090
Yeah, me too.
是啊，我也是。

1670
01:08:54.230 --> 01:08:56.150
And we did not have a lot of time.
而且我们时间不多。

1671
01:08:56.590 --> 01:08:58.030
We didn't have a lot of time to get this.
我们没有太多时间来完成这一幕。

1672
01:08:58.030 --> 01:08:58.890
The clock was ticking.
时间紧迫。

1673
01:08:59.170 --> 01:09:03.690
Yeah, exactly, because we didn't want to go into overtime for everyone, and it was the end of the day.
没错，因为我们不想让大家加班，而且当时已经是收工时间了。

1674
01:09:03.690 --> 01:09:10.110
And so Charles McDougal said to me, we're probably only going to do like two takes, maybe three.
所以查尔斯·麦克杜格尔对我说，我们可能只会拍两遍，顶多三遍。

1675
01:09:10.110 --> 01:09:17.770
But they gave me these ornaments, and my instruction was that my character has just lost it.
他们给了我这些装饰品，给我的指示是我的角色已经彻底崩溃了。

1676
01:09:17.890 --> 01:09:19.650
Michael has ruined Christmas.
迈克尔毁了圣诞节。

1677
01:09:20.150 --> 01:09:21.970
Kelly has kissed my man.
凯莉亲了我的男人。

1678
01:09:22.230 --> 01:09:24.790
Ryan is the king of the party planning committee.
瑞安成了派对策划委员会的国王。

1679
01:09:24.990 --> 01:09:25.570
Ah!
啊！

1680
01:09:25.950 --> 01:09:26.230
Right?
对吧？

1681
01:09:26.370 --> 01:09:26.650
Yes.
是的。

1682
01:09:26.650 --> 01:09:30.690
He said, I want you to take these ornaments and just throw them and shatter them.
他说，我要你拿着这些装饰品，直接扔出去把它们砸碎。

1683
01:09:30.830 --> 01:09:33.510
They were written in the script as glass ornaments.
剧本里写的是玻璃装饰品。

1684
01:09:33.710 --> 01:09:33.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1685
01:09:34.330 --> 01:09:35.870
They were not glass ornaments.
它们根本不是玻璃装饰品。

1686
01:09:36.150 --> 01:09:36.410
What?
什么？

1687
01:09:36.630 --> 01:09:37.490
Watch the scene.
看那场戏。

1688
01:09:37.630 --> 01:09:38.250
I throw them down.
我把它们扔下去。

1689
01:09:38.450 --> 01:09:40.530
They bounce straight up in the air.
它们直接弹回了空中。

1690
01:09:40.670 --> 01:09:41.450
What were they?
那是什么做的？

1691
01:09:41.450 --> 01:09:44.470
They were like some kind of plastic composite whatever.
它们好像是某种塑料复合材料之类的东西。

1692
01:09:44.870 --> 01:09:45.510
Oh, no.
哦，不。

1693
01:09:45.790 --> 01:09:47.670
So when you look, watch it, you guys.
所以你们看的时候留意一下。

1694
01:09:47.790 --> 01:09:49.250
You see them bounce in the air.
你们会看到它们在空中弹起。

1695
01:09:49.710 --> 01:09:51.970
I assumed, well, that makes sense.
我当时想，好吧，这倒也合理。

1696
01:09:51.970 --> 01:09:57.810
We did not have the budget to get special breakaway glass ornaments, and there's no way they would
我们没有预算去买那种特制的易碎玻璃装饰品，而且他们绝不可能

1697
01:09:57.810 --> 01:09:58.970
give you real glass.
给你真玻璃。

1698
01:09:59.610 --> 01:10:02.730
So these things bounced like a tennis ball.
所以这些东西像网球一样弹了起来。

1699
01:10:03.050 --> 01:10:05.090
And so Charles is like, cut.
于是查尔斯喊了停。

1700
01:10:05.190 --> 01:10:06.830
And he goes, okay, two things.
他说，好吧，有两件事。

1701
01:10:07.030 --> 01:10:09.630
One, we need you to stand closer to the wall.
第一，我们需要你站得离墙更近一点。

1702
01:10:09.750 --> 01:10:13.130
Like if you can in the scene, get as close to the wall as possible because that's where
就像在戏里那样，尽可能贴近墙壁，因为那是

1703
01:10:13.130 --> 01:10:15.690
the guy is with the soap coming down.
那个拿着肥皂的人走过来的地方。

1704
01:10:15.890 --> 01:10:16.090
Yeah.
好的。

1705
01:10:16.090 --> 01:10:17.610
The soap doesn't ball very far.
肥皂滚不了多远。

1706
01:10:17.810 --> 01:10:19.510
So we have another take.
所以我们又拍了一次。

1707
01:10:19.510 --> 01:10:21.810
And he's like, why aren't you breaking the ornaments?
他问我，为什么你不把装饰品弄碎？

1708
01:10:21.990 --> 01:10:22.990
I'm like, Charles, they're bouncing.
