01:16:07.730 --> 01:16:10.050
Her image wasn't on any monitors anywhere.
她的影像没有出现在任何地方的监视器上。

1873
01:16:10.410 --> 01:16:10.850
That's right.
没错。

1874
01:16:10.850 --> 01:16:13.470
And there was no chip in the digital camera.
而且数码相机里也没有存储卡。

1875
01:16:13.730 --> 01:16:15.230
So the flash goes off.
所以闪光灯亮起时。

1876
01:16:15.310 --> 01:16:16.810
It looks like Michael's taking a picture.
看起来像是迈克尔在拍照。

1877
01:16:16.970 --> 01:16:19.290
But there was actually never a picture taken.
但实际上根本没拍下照片。

1878
01:16:19.310 --> 01:16:19.910
Never a photo.
一张照片都没拍。

1879
01:16:19.910 --> 01:16:25.270
So they were very, very mindful of taking care of Kate in that moment.
所以他们当时非常、非常用心地照顾凯特。

1880
01:16:25.690 --> 01:16:29.750
Kate would go on as Meredith to take off her clothes.
凯特后来作为梅雷迪思脱掉了衣服。

1881
01:16:30.130 --> 01:16:30.830
And quite a bit.
而且脱了不少。

1882
01:16:30.930 --> 01:16:31.370
Quite a bit.
脱了不少。

1883
01:16:31.690 --> 01:16:37.090
One of my favorite, favorite things is that Kate's father wrote her a handwritten letter.
我最喜欢的事情之一，就是凯特的父亲给她写了一封亲笔信。

1884
01:16:37.090 --> 01:16:38.270
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1885
01:16:38.730 --> 01:16:43.170
And all it said, this is her father, who, you know, Kate is from Pennsylvania.
信上只写了——这是她父亲，你知道的，凯特来自宾夕法尼亚州。

1886
01:16:43.490 --> 01:16:48.790
And all it said was, dear Kate, stop taking your clothes off.
信上只写着：亲爱的凯特，别再脱衣服了。

1887
01:16:49.110 --> 01:16:50.010
Love, dad.
爱你的，爸爸。

1888
01:16:50.290 --> 01:16:51.470
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1889
01:16:52.670 --> 01:16:53.870
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1890
01:16:54.850 --> 01:16:56.430
What did Kate do?
凯特怎么做的？

1891
01:16:56.590 --> 01:16:57.830
How did she respond to that?
她是怎么回应的？

1892
01:16:57.930 --> 01:16:59.090
She was like, oh, man.
她说，天呐。

1893
01:16:59.550 --> 01:17:02.010
Now, is that her dad having a sense of humor?
那么，这是她爸爸在幽默吗？

1894
01:17:02.010 --> 01:17:04.610
Or is that him being like, seriously, stop it?
还是他真的在说，说真的，别再脱了？

1895
01:17:04.770 --> 01:17:05.550
I think both.
我觉得两者都有。

1896
01:17:05.710 --> 01:17:06.290
I think both.
我觉得两者都有。

1897
01:17:06.290 --> 01:17:06.770
All right.
好吧。

1898
01:17:06.890 --> 01:17:08.390
Should we talk about the parking lot?
我们要聊聊停车场的事吗？

1899
01:17:08.630 --> 01:17:10.090
We're almost done here.
我们快聊完了。

1900
01:17:10.690 --> 01:17:11.010
Yes.
好的。

1901
01:17:11.010 --> 01:17:12.370
Let's talk about the parking lot.
我们来聊聊停车场那场戏吧。

1902
01:17:12.490 --> 01:17:18.470
Because it is definitely one of the most magical moments that I remember in filming all nine years.
因为那绝对是我九年拍摄生涯中最神奇的时刻之一。

1903
01:17:18.470 --> 01:17:19.810
And we all say that.
我们大家都这么说。

1904
01:17:20.050 --> 01:17:20.310
Yeah.
没错。

1905
01:17:20.450 --> 01:17:23.910
People often ask, like, what were your favorite scenes?
人们经常问，你们最喜欢的场景是哪些？

1906
01:17:24.190 --> 01:17:26.910
And it's always hard to explain.
这总是很难解释。

1907
01:17:26.910 --> 01:17:30.650
Because sometimes your favorite scene, it doesn't seem like that exciting of a scene.
因为有时候你最喜欢的场景，看起来并没有那么令人兴奋。

1908
01:17:30.750 --> 01:17:34.110
But it's what happened behind the scenes that make it your favorite.
但正是幕后发生的事情让它成为了你的最爱。

1909
01:17:34.110 --> 01:17:36.010
And this parking lot scene is one of mine.
而这个停车场场景就是我的最爱之一。

1910
01:17:36.510 --> 01:17:36.990
Definitely.
绝对是。

1911
01:17:37.350 --> 01:17:37.830
Definitely.
绝对是。

1912
01:17:38.310 --> 01:17:38.590
Okay.
好吧。

1913
01:17:38.610 --> 01:17:40.250
So it's the end of the day.
那是收工的时候。

1914
01:17:40.410 --> 01:17:42.630
We have all of this real snow on the ground.
地上积满了真实的雪。

1915
01:17:42.950 --> 01:17:44.530
And everyone is leaving.
大家都准备离开了。

1916
01:17:44.530 --> 01:17:46.170
And everyone's in good spirits.
每个人的心情都很好。

1917
01:17:46.450 --> 01:17:47.670
And it's really nighttime.
而且天色已经完全黑了。

1918
01:17:48.030 --> 01:17:50.410
It was rare for us to ever work past 6 p.m.
我们很少会在下午6点以后工作。

1919
01:17:50.410 --> 01:17:51.690
So we always got excited.
所以我们总是很兴奋。

1920
01:17:52.010 --> 01:17:56.470
To walk out in the dark, I think, we all felt like we were up past our bedtime.
走在夜色中，我想我们都觉得自己像是过了睡觉时间还没睡。

1921
01:17:56.470 --> 01:17:59.170
But also, you have to remember, this is Los Angeles.
但你也要记住，这里是洛杉矶。

1922
01:17:59.430 --> 01:18:01.290
There's never snow on the ground.
地上从来不会有积雪。

1923
01:18:01.330 --> 01:18:06.550
So this is magical in itself that we have a parking lot full of snow.
所以停车场里铺满积雪本身就很神奇。

1924
01:18:06.550 --> 01:18:15.190
And as we're walking to the cars, I don't know, like, the shot you see, I'm actually in the front passenger seat of an SUV.
当我们走向汽车时，怎么说呢，你看到的那个镜头里，我其实坐在SUV的副驾驶座上。

1925
01:18:15.390 --> 01:18:17.530
But I'm only half in, like, the door's open.
但我只进去了一半，车门还开着。

1926
01:18:17.530 --> 01:18:22.190
But I remember one of the guys just picked up some snow and flung it at the other one.
我记得其中一个人抓起一把雪扔向另一个人。

1927
01:18:22.190 --> 01:18:27.570
And then they all started picking up snow and having this impromptu snowball fight.
然后他们都开始抓雪，打起了一场即兴的雪仗。

1928
01:18:27.910 --> 01:18:29.570
And everyone loved it.
大家都玩得很开心。

1929
01:18:29.630 --> 01:18:31.130
And they wanted us to keep doing it.
他们还想让我们继续打。

1930
01:18:31.210 --> 01:18:35.910
But it was just sort of like us just all hanging out in the snow.
但那感觉就像是我们大家在雪地里聚在一起玩耍。

1931
01:18:36.150 --> 01:18:36.430
Yeah.
没错。

1932
01:18:36.610 --> 01:18:38.610
And we turned into a bunch of kids.
我们都变成了小孩子。

1933
01:18:38.810 --> 01:18:39.770
We couldn't help it.
我们控制不住自己。

1934
01:18:39.910 --> 01:18:40.190
Yeah.
没错。

1935
01:18:40.350 --> 01:18:43.470
We were up past our bedtime with snow on the ground.
我们过了睡觉时间还在外面，地上还有积雪。

1936
01:18:43.870 --> 01:18:44.890
Fresh snow on the ground.
地上铺着新鲜的积雪。

1937
01:18:45.250 --> 01:18:46.410
It was so fun.
太好玩了。

1938
01:18:46.410 --> 01:18:53.290
And, you know, I have a picture of all of us together in the parking lot with Charles McDougal.
而且，你知道，我有一张我们所有人跟查尔斯·麦克道格在停车场拍的合影。

1939
01:18:53.710 --> 01:18:55.130
And it's great.
那张照片棒极了。

1940
01:18:55.390 --> 01:18:55.970
I love it.
我超喜欢。

1941
01:18:56.010 --> 01:18:56.870
I covet it.
我视若珍宝。

1942
01:18:57.070 --> 01:18:58.010
I covet it.
我视若珍宝。

1943
01:18:58.010 --> 01:18:58.130
I love that.
我喜欢那个。

1944
01:18:58.230 --> 01:18:59.050
I want to see it.
我想看看它。

1945
01:18:59.210 --> 01:18:59.490
Yeah.
好啊。

1946
01:18:59.750 --> 01:19:03.090
Well, this is why we have to make our scrapbook thingy, Angela.
安吉拉，这就是为什么我们得做那个剪贴簿之类的东西。

1947
01:19:03.350 --> 01:19:03.690
We do.
确实。

1948
01:19:03.730 --> 01:19:04.450
We should combine.
我们应该合在一起做。

1949
01:19:04.630 --> 01:19:05.670
Well, that's what we need to do.
嗯，这就是我们需要做的。

1950
01:19:05.750 --> 01:19:09.070
We need to compile and combine all of our stuff.
我们需要把我们所有的东西整理并汇编在一起。

1951
01:19:09.690 --> 01:19:12.690
And then make it so that we can both have what we both have.
然后我们要设法让我们俩都能拥有我们各自拥有的东西。

1952
01:19:13.230 --> 01:19:13.650
Yeah.
是啊。

1953
01:19:14.010 --> 01:19:14.370
Right?
对吧？

1954
01:19:14.570 --> 01:19:14.890
Yeah.
没错。

1955
01:19:15.150 --> 01:19:15.370
Yeah.
是啊。

1956
01:19:15.370 --> 01:19:17.770
Before we lose it all, we need to do it.
在我们失去这一切之前，我们得把它做了。

1957
01:19:18.390 --> 01:19:18.790
Okay.
好的。

1958
01:19:19.030 --> 01:19:19.710
It's 2020.
现在是2020年了。

1959
01:19:21.070 --> 01:19:22.350
We need to do this.
我们得完成这件事。

1960
01:19:22.430 --> 01:19:23.530
This is a goal for this year.
这是我们今年的目标。

1961
01:19:23.630 --> 01:19:25.390
I'm setting the goal for us this year.
我正在为我们设定今年的目标。

1962
01:19:25.530 --> 01:19:27.150
Well, you guys, she said it.
好了，各位，她都说了。

1963
01:19:27.410 --> 01:19:30.250
Now I've got to, like, Jenna's going to put me to task.
现在我必须得做了，珍娜会督促我的。

1964
01:19:30.410 --> 01:19:31.890
This episode was really special.
这一集真的很特别。

1965
01:19:31.990 --> 01:19:32.350
It was.
确实。

1966
01:19:32.450 --> 01:19:36.050
I really hope we did it justice because it means so much to us.
我真心希望我们没有辜负它，因为它对我们意义重大。

1967
01:19:36.250 --> 01:19:41.350
These episodes are almost harder for me than other ones because there's so much emotion
对我来说，这些剧集几乎比其他的更难，因为其中蕴含了太多的情感，

1968
01:19:41.350 --> 01:19:42.170
attached to it.
与它紧密相连。

1969
01:19:42.310 --> 01:19:44.130
There's so much that happens in the scene.
这一幕里发生了太多事情。

1970
01:19:44.130 --> 01:19:49.550
And not only, like, is it special to us personally, but it was, like, a big moment for our characters.
而且这不仅对我们个人来说很特别，对我们的角色来说也是一个重要的时刻。

1971
01:19:49.850 --> 01:19:50.010
Yeah.
是啊。

1972
01:19:50.010 --> 01:19:59.610
And just that moment at the end, that snowball fight, that is just a group of people who love each other, who are all getting to hang out,
还有最后那个打雪仗的时刻，那只是一群彼此相爱的人聚在一起玩耍，

1973
01:19:59.630 --> 01:20:02.210
and we just happen to be on a TV show together.
而我们恰好一起出演了一部电视剧。

1974
01:20:02.390 --> 01:20:02.710
Yeah.
没错。

1975
01:20:02.710 --> 01:20:04.130
It's just a really special moment.
那真是一个非常特别的时刻。

1976
01:20:04.130 --> 01:20:06.810
And I love that they let that be how it ended.
我很高兴他们让那一幕成为了结局。

1977
01:20:07.190 --> 01:20:17.890
And that's really how it felt when we left this show, that we were just a bunch of friends who happened to be on a TV show together because we were friends.
当我们离开这部剧时，感觉确实如此，我们只是一群恰好一起拍戏的朋友，因为我们本来就是朋友。

1978
